  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements:</p><p><strong>Statement I:</strong> If<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>be the total energy of a satellite moving around the earth, then its potential energy will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>.</p><p><strong>Statement II:</strong> The kinetic energy of a satellite revolving in an orbit is equal to the half the magnitude of total energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math>.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "2GdJT",
      "text": "Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pmkTI",
      "text": "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "QRBnH",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are correct",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "aGj8b",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;be the mass of the satellite.</p><p>The potential energy of the satellite is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>The velocity of the satellite is given by&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>Kinetic energy is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>The total mechanical energy is the sum of potential and kinetic energy. So,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, both the statements are false.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
